<BehaviorPatch #track.r_2_0_2_6_-_0_7_-_0_2_-_2_2_2_0_-_e_x_t_e_n_d_-_x_n_l_-_c_o_r_e_-_d_s_l_-_s_y_n_t_a_x.behavior_patch.xnl-dotted-tag apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" version="1" { capability = "xnl-dotted-tag" } (
  <Mutations [
    <Upsert { selector = "behavior://xnl-dotted-tag/requirements/dotted-tag-grammar" } (
      <Requirement #dotted-tag-grammar (
        <Statement ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3E>
        The parser SHALL accept dotted fully-qualified tag names of the form `seg(.seg)*` where each segment matches the existing identifier grammar `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*`, e.g. `&lt;dg.materials.CrudTable #users-table&gt;`.
        </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3E>
        <Suites [
          <Suite #dotted-tag { name = "Dotted tag grammar" } (
            <Cases [
              <Case #parse-dotted-tag (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3F>
                Source `&lt;dg.materials.CrudTable #t { pageSize = 20 }&gt;`.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3F>
                <When ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3G>
                parseXnl parses the source.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3G>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3H>
                Parsing SHALL succeed and the node tag SHALL be the joined string `dg.materials.CrudTable`.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3H>
              )>
              <Case #segment-grammar (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3J>
                A tag with an empty segment, leading dot, or trailing dot (e.g. `&lt;a..b&gt;`, `&lt;.a&gt;`, `&lt;a.&gt;`).
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3J>
                <When ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3K>
                parseXnl parses the source.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3K>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3M>
                The parser SHALL raise a parse error and SHALL NOT silently truncate the tag.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3M>
              )>
              <Case #full-combination (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3N>
                A dotted-tag node combining `#id`, metadata, `{...}` attributes, `(...)` extend section, and `[...]` array body.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3N>
                <When ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3P>
                parseXnl parses the source.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3P>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3Q>
                All sections SHALL parse exactly as they do for single-segment tags.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3Q>
              )>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
    )>
    <Upsert { selector = "behavior://xnl-dotted-tag/requirements/tag-string-compat" } (
      <Requirement #tag-string-compat (
        <Statement ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3R>
        `DataElementNode.tag` and `TextElementNode.tag` SHALL remain plain strings holding the joined dotted form; single-segment tag behavior SHALL be unchanged.
        </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3R>
        <Suites [
          <Suite #compat { name = "Tag type compatibility" } (
            <Cases [
              <Case #single-segment-unchanged (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3S>
                Any existing document using single-segment tags.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3S>
                <When ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3T>
                The full test suite runs after the change.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3T>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3V>
                All existing parser/formatter/loader/import/path/mutation tests SHALL pass unchanged.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3V>
              )>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
    )>
    <Upsert { selector = "behavior://xnl-dotted-tag/requirements/roundtrip-fidelity" } (
      <Requirement #roundtrip-fidelity (
        <Statement ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3W>
        Formatters SHALL print dotted tags verbatim so that parse -> stringify -> parse is stable for dotted-tag documents.
        </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3W>
        <Suites [
          <Suite #roundtrip { name = "Roundtrip fidelity" } (
            <Cases [
              <Case #stringify-dotted (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3X>
                A parsed node with tag `dg.materials.CrudTable`.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3X>
                <When ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3Y>
                The document is stringified with the default and line-block formatters.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3Y>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3Z>
                The output SHALL contain `&lt;dg.materials.CrudTable` and reparsing SHALL yield an equal AST.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH3Z>
              )>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
    )>
    <Upsert { selector = "behavior://xnl-dotted-tag/requirements/tooling-regression" } (
      <Requirement #tooling-regression (
        <Statement ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH40>
        path resolution, mutation diff/apply, and loader/import SHALL treat dotted tags as opaque tag strings with no behavior change.
        </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH40>
        <Suites [
          <Suite #tooling { name = "Tooling regression" } (
            <Cases [
              <Case #mutation-on-dotted (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH41>
                Two documents differing in an attribute of a dotted-tag node.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH41>
                <When ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH42>
                diffNodes produces mutations and applyMutations applies them.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH42>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH43>
                The mutation SHALL address the node correctly and the result SHALL equal the target document.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH43>
              )>
              <Case #path-on-dotted (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH44>
                A document containing a dotted-tag node with `#id`.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH44>
                <When ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH45>
                XNL.path resolve/set operates on a path through that node.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH45>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH46>
                Resolution SHALL behave identically to single-segment tags.
                </?01M1W1C2D20QCH7QV5T81DQH46>
              )>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
    )>
  ]>
)>
